<%# Sender, subject, freshness. Every part is a direct child of the grid, the
    way a feed row's is, so the freshness takes a column of its own on desktop
    and folds under the subject on mobile.

    The whole line is the link, and it opens the sender's own email rather
    than the reader's rendering of it: their confirm button is in there. %>
<li class="pen__item">
  <%= link_to row.path, class: "pen__line pen__line--open" do %>
    <span class="pen__sender"><%= row.sender %></span>
    <span class="pen__subject"><%= row.subject %></span>
    <span class="pen__freshness"><%= row.freshness %></span>
  <% end %>
</li>
